<!--
  Entitlements for the hardened runtime, applied by `scripts/macos-bundle.sh` when it ad-hoc signs
  the bundle on macOS.

  Deliberately empty. The application reads and writes files the user points it at, spawns
  processes, and talks to a unix socket under $HOME, none of which the hardened runtime restricts.
  It is not sandboxed, so no `com.apple.security.*` grant is required, and adding one that is not
  needed only widens what a future signature vouches for.

  This file is the seam for FR-017: adopting a Developer ID certificate and notarization edits
  this file (plus the signing identity in `scripts/macos-bundle.sh`) rather than restructuring the
  bundle. Notarization additionally requires an Apple account and a repository secret, which
  FR-016 forbids today; see `docs/development/macos-packaging.md`.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
